---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
---
<Page
  title="Participant Guide — IEEE × IET CICADE"
  bodyClass="world-public page-guide"
  currentPage="/guide"
>
  <div class="shell--narrow page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        <svg class="eyebrow__o" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#o-mini"/></svg>
        <span>Handbook</span>
      </p>
      <h1>Participant Guide</h1>
      <p class="lede">Everything you need to know about CICADE — from registration to the grand finale.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose stack stack-lg">

      <section>
        <h2>What is CICADE?</h2>
        <p>
          CICADE (<em>pronounced sih-KAY-deh</em>) is the joint CTF hackathon hosted by the <strong>IEEE</strong> and <strong>IET Student Chapters</strong> at Thapar Institute of Engineering &amp; Technology, Patiala.
        </p>
        <p>
          Teams compete across four participation modes — SEED, CORE, FRONTIER, and FORGE — building solutions to real engineering and technology challenges over a 36–72 hour sprint.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Timeline</h2>
        <div class="panel">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Phase</th><th>Date</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Registration opens</td><td><time>15 October 2026</time></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Registration closes</td><td><time>28 November 2026, 23:59 IST</time></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Screening results</td><td><time>5 December 2026</time></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Mentorship calls</td><td><time>10–15 December 2026</time></td></tr>
              <tr><td>CICADE hackathon sprint</td><td><time>20–22 December 2026</time></td></tr>
              <tr><td>Grand Finale &amp; prize ceremony</td><td><time>22 December 2026</time></td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Rules &amp; Eligibility</h2>
        <h3>General Rules</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>All team members must be currently enrolled students.</li>
          <li>Each team must have exactly 4 members (FORGE: 4–6).</li>
          <li>At least one female-identifying member is mandatory per team.</li>
          <li>Teams may not switch tracks after registration.</li>
          <li>All code must be written during the hackathon sprint (screening submissions are separate).</li>
          <li>Plagiarism or misrepresentation of work will result in immediate disqualification.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What You Can Bring</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Pre-built hardware components (must be declared at check-in)</li>
          <li>Existing open-source libraries (must be cited)</li>
          <li>Design files, wireframes, and research notes</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>What You Cannot Use</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Previously submitted or publicly published projects</li>
          <li>Code written before the sprint begins</li>
          <li>AI-generated code without disclosure (must declare tools used)</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>On-site Logistics</h2>
        <h3>Venue</h3>
        <p>
          Thapar Institute of Engineering &amp; Technology (TIET)<br/>
          Patiala, Punjab 147004, India
        </p>

        <h3>Accommodation</h3>
        <p>
          TIET hostels will be available for outstation participants. Accommodation requests must be submitted via the registration form. Accommodation is provided on a first-come, first-served basis.
        </p>

        <h3>Meals</h3>
        <p>
          All registered participants receive meals throughout the event — breakfast, lunch, dinner, and midnight snacks during the sprint.
        </p>

        <h3>What to Bring</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Laptop and charger</li>
          <li>Valid college ID</li>
          <li>Hardware components (declared in advance)</li>
          <li>Comfortable clothes for a 48-hour sprint</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Code of Conduct</h2>
        <p>
          CICADE is committed to providing a safe, inclusive, and welcoming environment for all participants regardless of gender, sexual orientation, disability, ethnicity, religion, or technical experience level.
        </p>
        <p>
          Harassment, discrimination, or intimidating behaviour of any kind will result in immediate removal from the event without refund or appeal.
        </p>
        <p>
          To report a concern, contact any organiser in person or email <a href="mailto:safety@cicade.thapar.edu">safety@cicade.thapar.edu</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <div class="grid grid--2">
          <div>
            <h3>General Enquiries</h3>
            <p><a href="mailto:hello@cicade.thapar.edu">hello@cicade.thapar.edu</a></p>
            <p><a href="https://discord.gg/SsVuHQzX8" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discord community</a></p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Sponsorships</h3>
            <p><a href="mailto:sponsors@cicade.thapar.edu">sponsors@cicade.thapar.edu</a></p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Mentors</h3>
            <p><a href="mailto:mentors@cicade.thapar.edu">mentors@cicade.thapar.edu</a></p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>FORGE Track</h3>
            <p><a href="mailto:forge@cicade.thapar.edu">forge@cicade.thapar.edu</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</Page>
